.IX Title "Passwd 3pm"
.TH Passwd 3pm 1998-08-17 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Crypt::Passwd \- Perl wrapper around the UFC Crypt
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 1
\&  use Crypt::Passwd;
\&  
\&  $crypted_password = unix_std_crypt("password", "salt");
\&  $ultrix_password = unix_ext_crypt("password", "salt");
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
This module provides an interface layer between Perl 5 and Michael
Glad's UFC Crypt library.
.PP
The interface is comprised in two functions, described below.
.PP
\&\fIunix_std_crypt(passwd, salt)\fR provides an interface to the traditional
\&\fBcrypt()\fR function, as implemented by the UFC library. It returns the crypted
password, perturbed with the salt.
.PP
\&\fIunix_ext_crypt(passwd, salt)\fR provides the interface to the \fBcrypt16()\fR
function, present in Ultrix and Digital Unix systems as implemented
in the UFC Library.
.PP
This code is provided as is, with no warranties. It is subject to the same
terms and conditions that Perl and the UFC Crypt library.
.SH AUTHOR
.IX Header "AUTHOR"
Luis E. Munoz, lem@cantv.net
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBperl\fR\|(1), \fBcrypt\fR\|(3), \fBfcrypt\fR\|(3), \fBcrypt16\fR\|(3)
